# SYS-000 — System reference title

> **Summary:** What this reference manual documents about the live system.
> **Epistemic:** How the system works as wired today — components,
> connections, boundaries, data flows.
> **Pragmatic:** Use to onboard, audit, or plan changes.
> **Audience:** Agents · Oracles

> **A system document is a reference manual, not a plan.** It describes what
> *is*, not what *could be* (that is `blueprints/`, STD-001 §2).

---

## Scope

What this reference covers, and what is explicitly out of scope.

## Architecture

The components, their connections, and the boundaries between them. Concrete:
repos, services, protocols, data flows.

## Accuracy

Known staleness, if any, and the debt entry that tracks it. A reference that
contradicts reality is a defect, not a plan.

